Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-judgment-replacement.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not an individualized-person-centered-care-replacement.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not an inflexible-standard.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline then it is recommended that the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not cause a rapid-opioid-taper.
If there is an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline then it is recommended that the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not cause an abrupt-opioid-discontinuation.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-practice-law.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-practice-regulation.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not a clinical-practice-policy.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not an FDA-approved-labeling-substitute.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not apply during a sickle-cell-disease-pain.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not apply during a cancer-related-pain.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not apply during a palliative-care.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline does not apply during an end-of-life-care.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline is not an opioid-use-disorder-medication-guideline.
